# Type: Defect regression

@regression
Feature: nmg-sdlc steering and skill-contract documentation stays aligned
  The standalone plugin's steering previously retained its former monorepo
  identity, unresolved project placeholders, and inactive Codex resource claims.
  The fix aligns repo-specific guidance with the live plugin while preserving
  intentional marketplace and legacy compatibility references.

  @regression
  Scenario: Standalone project identity is correct
    Given the standalone manifest identifies the plugin and repository as "nmg-sdlc"
    When a maintainer audits README, AGENTS, steering, active skills, and shared references
    Then current repo-specific guidance identifies the plugin as "nmg-sdlc"
    And "nmg-plugins" remains only for the external marketplace, installed cache, supported legacy layout, test fixtures, or historical records

  @regression
  Scenario: Repo-specific steering contains no unresolved placeholders
    Given the repository is a prompt-based Codex plugin without a database or UI layer
    When the repo-specific technical and structure steering documents are inspected
    Then no unresolved convention, example, token, or equivalent placeholder standards remain
    And inapplicable database and UI design-token sections are absent

  @regression
  Scenario: Skill and agent contract guidance matches active files
    Given active skills and reusable agent prompts define the current Codex resource shape
    When steering guidance is compared with those files and the plugin manifest
    Then the documented skill, agent, and plugin metadata contracts match the live files
    And the regression test fails if inactive "allowedTools" or unsupported reusable-agent execution-control claims return
